 HISTORY                                                          3016 1451
 -------                                                          3016 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  3016 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA. The        3016 1451
 inelastic scattering cross section libraries for Si in           3016 1451
 alpha-quartz, SiO2-alpha, were fully developed using ab-initio   3016 1451
 lattice dynamics (AILD) methods [1]. Seven temperatures are      3016 1451
 available in this library. The Full Law Analysis Scattering      3016 1451
 System Hub (FLASSH) was used to produce MT = 2 (coherent) and    3016 1451
 MT = 4 data [2]. By convention, MAT=3016 and ZA=3116 are used    3016 1451
 for Si in SiO2-alpha. The phonon DOS used in this evaluation was 3016 1451
 generated using a new AILD model for SiO2-alpha. The trigonal    3016 1451
 structure, belonging to the P3_221 space group (#154), was       3016 1451
 modeled in VASP [3-5] using the LDA exchange-correlation         3016 1451
 functional with a 600eV plane-wave energy cutoff and an 8x8x6    3016 1451
 Monkhorst-Pack k-point mesh. The phonon density of states was    3016 1451
 generated using a 2x2x2 supercell in PHONON [6] via the dynamical3016 1451
 matrix method. Experimental lattice data was used to calculate   3016 1451
 the coherent elastic cross section [7-9]. The isotopic total free3016 1451
 atom cross sections were taken from MF = 3, MT = 2 of the        3016 1451
 ENDF/B-VIII.0 nuclide evaluations [10] at 1.0E-05 eV.            3016 1451
